      "edges": [
        {
          "from": "evidence_000017",
          "to": "claim_000003",
          "mapping_id": "mapping_000003",
          "relation": "context",
          "explanation": "This paragraph defines the five evaluation conditions, including the full-raw-data baselines and the full-raw-data-plus-correct-visualization condition. It provides the comparison scope needed to interpret the claim’s phrase 'relative to baselines with full raw data.'",
          "source_parts_used": [
            "source_text"
          ],
          "relation_status": "recorded"
        },
        {
          "from": "evidence_000053",
          "to": "claim_000003",
          "mapping_id": "mapping_000003",
          "relation": "supports",
          "explanation": "Figure 2 directly supports the claim for the cluster-identification task. Its caption states that visualization improves GPT 4.1 and Claude 3.5’s ability to detect the number of clusters, and the supplied visual reading indicates that the Data & Correct bars are generally above the raw-data baselines for 3- to 5-cluster datasets. This is direct evidence that adding the correct visualization helps both models relative to full-data baselines.",
          "source_parts_used": [
            "caption",
            "visual_observation"
          ],
          "relation_status": "recorded"
        },
        {
          "from": "evidence_000037",
          "to": "claim_000003",
          "mapping_id": "mapping_000003",
          "relation": "supports",
          "explanation": "Figure 3 supports the claim for the parabolic-trend task. The caption explicitly says visualization improves GPT 4.1 and Claude 3.5’s ability to identify parabolic trends in datasets. Although it also notes that at higher subtlety the correct plot alone can outperform data-plus-plot, the caption still supports the narrower claim that correct visualization improves understanding relative to the baseline conditions without an accurate plot.",
          "source_parts_used": [
            "caption"
          ],
          "relation_status": "recorded"
        },
        {
          "from": "evidence_000008",
          "to": "claim_000003",
          "mapping_id": "mapping_000003",
          "relation": "supports",
          "explanation": "Figure 4 extends the same pattern to outlier identification. Its caption states that visualization improves GPT 4.1 and Claude 3.5’s ability to identify the correct outlier, with declines especially without accurate visuals as subtlety increases. This broadens support for the claim from one task to multiple dataset-understanding tasks.",
          "source_parts_used": [
            "caption"
          ],
          "relation_status": "recorded"
        },
        {
          "from": "evidence_000032",
          "to": "claim_000003",
          "mapping_id": "mapping_000003",
          "relation": "qualifies",
          "explanation": "This paragraph qualifies the strength and uniformity of the effect in the cluster task: with 2-cluster data, GPT improves only slightly with accurate visualizations, while Claude identifies 2 clusters across conditions. That means the claim is best interpreted as an overall study result rather than a strict every-setting improvement of large magnitude.",
          "source_parts_used": [
            "source_text"
          ],
          "relation_status": "recorded"
        }
      ],
      "qualifications": [
        "The evidence supports a study-level trend, not a universal improvement in every individual setting.",
        "In the easy 2-cluster setting, Claude shows little or no gain across conditions, and in the parabolic-trend task the caption notes that correct-plot-only can outperform data-plus-correct-plot at higher subtlety."
      ],
